{
	"desc": "The Relic look (docs/decisions/0011-mantle-look.md). In a match a Relic wearer looks like the class's original Hunter (`wardens`: gender, folk, face, hair, palette; the class's gear and silhouette come from the archetype), nudged by the player's own person (Save look, PlayerLook). Each slider (0..1, 0.5 = neutral) moves its model factor by at most `sliders.<key>.clamp` either way (a Hunter's own `clamp` block overrides it); at home the player is their own person, with `own_k` times that range and their own colours. Each colour pick pulls the Hunter's colour `pull` of the way in HSV, never more than `hue` / `sat` / `val` (a Warden's `tint` block overrides it), so signature colours stay. Hitboxes never read any of this. `presets` set the face sliders as a starting point. Gender is the base character's (OWNER_REVIEW item 39; 'robot' builds on the male body).",
